config BR2_PACKAGE_IMAGE_STORAGE
	bool "image-storage"
	help
	  No upstream, no install content - this package exists only to
	  carry LINUX_CONFIG_FIXUPS for the filesystems the image's own
	  storage needs the kernel to support: EROFS for the read-only
	  root slot, and ext4 plus f2fs for the data partition (S15data
	  and system-install can format it as either). Board kernel
	  defconfigs do not carry these; ext4 tends to be on already,
	  EROFS and f2fs generally are not.

	  Enabled unconditionally by the image profile - every image
	  needs its root and data filesystems to actually mount.
